  "title": "Community models grow into video",
  "summary": "Community video publishing, new image and multimodal models, and coding-agent integrations led a day of catalog and API work.\n\nPublishers can register and test synchronous video models from the dashboard, Account API, or `polli my-models`. The models accept prompts, durations, and optional reference media, and can be called through video or image generation endpoints. Video requests now require whole-second durations from 1 to 120. Community embedding publishing was fixed, while queued listing changes and their effective dates are easier to see.\n\nFLUX.2 Pro and Flex add image generation and multi-reference editing, with support for up to eight and ten reference images respectively. The new `thinkingmachines/inkling` model accepts text, images, and audio, and supports tools, JSON, and streaming. GLM-5.3 Flash moved to Fireworks and no longer requires paid access; Grok 4.6 moved to Azure with a 200K-token published context limit. With GPT Realtime 2 retired on August 31, its old ID remains a compatibility alias for 2.1.\n\nOfficial and community model lists now default to Popular, ranked by distinct users with successful requests over seven days. Community tabs reflect the categories actually in the catalog, including video or embeddings when present. A new MCPs tab makes servers searchable alongside their endpoints and billing details; the API exposes the same MCP pricing information. Smaller changes tighten model metadata and text leaderboard counts.",
